;; Native SysML projects each generation contract to its existing obligation.
;; This readback reports evidence coverage; it does not prove the invariant.
(relation commitBoundaryFact (boundary obligation invariant) (("gerbil-bootstrap-module-custody" "T-GERBIL" "Unchanged per-module source/options/parent/runtime and exact output bytes require the immutable same-run completed process witness; queued, partial, failed or unknown outputs never qualify. Child records do not become recipe-stage PASS. Publication is serialized while independent compiler processes overlap within a host-derived envelope.") ("gerbil-resource-and-source-context" "T-GERBIL" "The existing managed source delta preserves caller runtime options before authoritative install mappings. Source overlays enter action identity rather than the physical workspace key. Only a target matching its previous witnessed input may be replaced. Compiler semantic context includes GAMBOPT; independent-action job capacity does not change it. Parent plus J one-processor compiler jobs uses a conservative 2J+1 scheduling envelope, not an OS-thread quota.") ("callback-nonlocal-exit-custody" "T-CATALOG" "A throw from ___call carries explicit control origin through both SFUN sites. All three generated families skip conversion recovery for thrown control, execute existing cleanup and propagate the unchanged status. Declarations and function-table signatures migrate with the wrappers. Reaching a Scheme continuation can precede physical C return: still-active callback banks remain roots across GC until their own unwind. Never restore an obsolete Scheme frame or prematurely drop its bank.") ("unpublished-stage1-lookup-custody" "T-GERBIL" "Only a completed matching stage1 proof may remain in the consumer lookup path. Before retrying an unqualified stage1, leased and quiescent ownership permits withdrawing its core/static outputs and Gerbil launchers by inode move into the attempt evidence directory. Preserve completed bootstrap and Gambit runtime payloads. Never overwrite retained failed custody or move outputs of an unknown live producer.") ("generated-host-compilation-unit" "T-ORIGINAL" "The existing profile single-host=0 enables single-host with no label-count limit; zero does not disable it. Compile-unit structure, frontend generation and independent-action scheduling are distinct responsibilities. Any proposed host partition must preserve PointId/FrameSpec, cross-host tail transfer, root maps and multi-shot continuation interpretation rather than changing a test's acceptance context.") ("compiler-job-budget" "T-COHORT" "Qualified native core compiler actions start one Scheme processor per Make job. Initial processor sum <= active jobs <= J; configured target Scheme SMP features are unchanged. This is not an OS-thread quota or a claim about arbitrary effectful compile-time code or interpreted compiler adapters") ("target-feature-dependency" "T-PRODUCTS" "One existing Configure source exports the target prelude and generation options into its existing feature header; module C depends on that header. C source edits do not change it; configuration changes cannot silently reuse unqualified generated C") ("configured-tool-lifetime" "T-COHORT" "Compiler clean removes generated compiler/runtime products but retains configuration-owned tool templates and launchers; their existing dependencies still rebuild on configuration/source changes") ("content-stable-stamp" "T-INCREMENTAL" "The non-Git working source keeps the stamp timestamp when its bytes are unchanged, without changing stamp contents or version semantics") ("generated-publication-family" "T-PRODUCTS" "Default publication and configured SMP outputs carry distinct target-feature and source-location contexts. Changed Scheme/native embedded bodies regenerate their default C and all downstream descriptors. Never copy profile-specific SMP C over default publication or normalize observable source paths away") ("thread-lock-lease" "T-ORIGINAL" "All successful lock acquisitions terminate through helper release before external interrupt dispatch; retry releases before reacquisition; the decision callback performs internal queue operations only") ("shared-fifo-guard" "T-ORIGINAL" "Both endpoint constructors receive the same mutex before peer/shared FIFO publication; predicate read, registration, publication and close use the same guard") ("native-producer-ancestry" "T-PRODUCER" "Unchanged actual native bootstrap event and requalification witnesses join the current producer identity; existing generation consumer leases it and executes a real map test") ("checked-result-control" "T-ORIGINAL" "Constant -1 multiplication returns the checked-negation success predicate and writes a numeric result only on success; generated C reads it only along the success edge. Minimum fixnum takes the existing fallback/exception edge. CONSTX delegates to the same CONSTY owner") ("gerbil-build-surface" "T-GERBIL" "Preserved namespaces and exported contracts remain usable through existing Gerbil build frontdoors; compiler CLI, macro phase, module linkage and new native cohort are coherent") ("compiler-context" "T-ORIGINAL" "One compilation action owns p1 and full-buffered artifact output; test execution independently inherits requested p3 and unchanged console settings. Existing namespace and original test bodies/caps remain unchanged") ("reconstruction-roots" "M-REFINE" "Every installed heap key/value is scanned throughout partial construction; final weak/index policy and reconstruction debt publish after the payload stores") ("context-initialization-permit" "M-REFINE" "Only the first primordial incarnation or a current INITIALIZING resize reservation with matching range, slot phase, generation and startup state may initialize context storage; admission precedes incarnation, bindings and sync writes") ("checked-vector-increment" "T-ORIGINAL" "Safe specialization evaluates operands once, validates increment and old element only after vector/index admission, then performs one unsafe atomic mutation or the authoritative Scheme error fallback")))
(relation commitBoundaryCovered (scenario boundary obligation))
;; Concrete ownership refinements are projected from native SysML. The route
;; preserves existing model premises; evidence availability is not their proof.
(relation commitOwnershipRouteFact (boundary model receipt premise obligation) (("thread-lock-lease" "models/gambit/ended_interrupt_lock.qnt" "evidence/model-results/ended-interrupt-lock.json" "acquire/propagate/observe; propagate closes locked in fixed state; exceptional termination does not preserve the lock" "T-ORIGINAL") ("shared-fifo-guard" "models/gambit/pipe_close_wait.qnt" "evidence/model-results/pipe-close-wait.json" "shared=true before checkEmpty/acquireWriter; registerWait atomically releases predicate lock; bounded one-direction conservation only" "T-ORIGINAL") ("native-producer-ancestry" "none:identity/source-refinement" "evidence/research/revision-admission/ownership-bootstrap-producer.json" "Distinct native reference; exact profile/input/generated/runtime/log witnesses; no duplicate QNT or Lean obligation" "T-PRODUCER") ("checked-result-control" "none:sequential-delegation-source-law-and-native-regression" "evidence/research/revision-admission/checked-predicate-results.json" "For multiplier -1, success iff x differs from MIN_FIX; then out=-x. On failure the output is not consumed. Existing negation helper owns both outcomes; no duplicate QNT or Lean state machine" "T-ORIGINAL") ("gerbil-build-surface" "dev/architecture/toolchain/models/sysml/gerbil-module-build.sysml; existing build assurance/QNT/Lean obligations remain owned there" "evidence/research/revision-admission/gerbil-build-contract.json" "Planning/front-end/readiness/execution preserve their actual source-duty edges; unchanged Scheme namespaces do not imply compiler-option, phase, ABI or artifact identity equivalence" "T-GERBIL") ("compiler-context" "GerbilModuleBuild::execution and existing toolchain resource obligations" "evidence/research/revision-admission/construction-results.json" "Different execution roles have separate resource and artifact ownership; test population is not lowered to make compilation pass" "T-ORIGINAL") ("reconstruction-roots" "dev/refactoring/modern-c/models/quint/hash_index_owner.qnt; existing HashIndexOwner Lean transport premise" "evidence/research/revision-admission/construction-protocol.recipe.json" "QNT owns the partial-store/relocation/commit schedule; Lean owns the existing conditional semantic transport law; the native adapter must establish scanned references and policy publication" "M-REFINE") ("context-initialization-permit" "Existing runtime_roles.qnt frozen-origin and participant premises; initialization is a C source refinement, not another schedule or Lean theorem" "evidence/research/revision-admission/context-initialization-results.json" "The real setup callers are initial VM setup and the closed resize coordinator; callbacks cannot recreate an already admitted live origin even when no cleanup payload is in flight" "M-REFINE") ("checked-vector-increment" "Existing Scheme primitive specialization contract and native counterexamples; no duplicate QNT or Lean scheduler" "evidence/research/revision-admission/construction-results.json" "Short-circuit index checks precede element access; rejected operations preserve the vector; default and explicit deltas return the old value" "T-ORIGINAL")))
