(relation commitMigrationFact (boundary obligation category preserved replaceable admission) (("scheme-language-contract" "Q-MULTISHOT" "semantic" "Observable Scheme control, proper tail calls, multi-shot continuation, dynamic-wind, shared identity and GC root correctness" "Internal frame, root, worker, scheduler and calling representations" "Actual interpreter/compiler/continuation/root tests under the new cohort; a stale binary or historical pass is not evidence") ("foreign-consumer-migration" "Q-FFI" "migration" "Root/resource custody, allocation reloading, result and exception semantics at changed Scheme/C boundaries" "C signatures, function tables, marker/root APIs and layouts; migrate all producers and consumers together" "No blanket old ABI requirement; list actual consumers and validate them under the new declarations/runtime") ("internal-responsibility-retirement" "Q-RETIRE" "retirement" "One canonical semantic/ownership authority and C portability" "Carrier-owned fields, old visitor paths, duplicated locks and old helper interfaces" "Delete obsolete paths after actual generator/caller/scanner/exit consumers migrate; no parallel compatibility layer") ("binary-cohort-admission" "Q-FFI" "artifact" "Only representation-coherent code and data may execute together" "Previous binary objects/modules may be discarded and rebuilt" "Default rebuilt cohort; old binaries need actual rejection or specific layout/signature evidence. Version and size checks alone are insufficient")))
